# Intent: The regional fix for the private network (the last open item of the old firmware). Two nodes start a handshake through a relay only when both sit on the same relay region: a node sends to a peer through its own home relay and the peer listens on its own. The client's default home region differs from a hub on another region, so a handshake the unit started failed and worked only when the hub spoke first. The old firmware pinned one region by hand (preferred_derp_region = 1). Here the unit learns the hub's region from the network map (the peer entry of the saved hub address) and moves its home relay there once (maipai_tailnet_core.h mt_region_wanted, at most 3 moves a boot and 60 s apart, tested on the host), then saves the region (NVS key derp, u16, written from the timer task which has an internal stack) so the next start begins there and needs no move. The move itself is a new library call, microlink_set_home_derp_region(), in the second library patch firmware/tailnet/microlink-region.patch (applied by scripts/fw-tailnet.sh after microlink.patch); it reuses the steps the client's own relay-region override takes. self.tailnet.status gains relay (the unit's home region) and hub_relay (the hub's). Cost: no new task or buffer; two small stack structures (about 250 bytes) on the timer task while it runs the two-second check, 2 bytes of NVS.
# Placement: unit (the robot's own travel client; works with the host off); library patch outside the unit tree
# Upstream: bot patch 147 (preferred_derp_region = 1) of the old firmware, generalized; components/microlink of the pinned client (MIT), see firmware/tailnet/microlink-region.patch
# Check after a flash: needs a real join (the owner's one-time key and the hub's private address): with the hub's relay region different from the unit's default, the log says 'moving the home relay to the hub's region' once, self.tailnet.status shows relay equal to hub_relay, and the unit's first message to the hub gets through without the hub speaking first; the next start logs no move.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_TAILNET.

